Vikram and Betal: The Greedy Judge

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a judge who was known for making decisions,” said Betal. “But he was also very greedy.”

One day, two men came to him with a dispute over a piece of land.

Both claimed it belonged to them.

The greedy judge secretly took money from one of the men.

The next day, he gave the judgment in favor of the man who paid him.

The other man was sad but did not give up.

He went to the king and told him everything.

The king called the judge and asked him to explain.

The judge could not answer properly.

The king realized the truth and removed the judge from his position.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, why did the judge lose his position?”

Vikram replied, “Because greed made him unfair and dishonest.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Greed leads to injustice.
